cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you cite this verification artifact, please cite the specific archived version you
  checked, not the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the
  "Archival" section in README.md.
title: >-
  minimal-uniformity-three: machine-checked companion to "Minimal uniformity of the
  non-Archimedean vertex types in unit-edge tilings"
abstract: >-
  The verification artifact for the paper's claims: the minimal uniformity of all ten
  non-Archimedean vertex species, proved to be 3, 3, 3, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 7 and 10. Lower
  bounds are exhaustive scans of Delaney-Dress symbol catalogues — DRAT-certified
  complete at up to two vertex orbits (24 UNSAT obligations over the tier-1
  certification universe, kissat-solved and drat-trim-verified), cross-validated by an
  orbit-bounded generator walk beyond — sharpened by corner-word enumerations, a chamber
  bound and stabiliser counting; upper bounds are rigid explicit tilings re-derived from
  their canonical keys in exact rational and cyclotomic arithmetic, with closure decided
  by vanishing sums of roots of unity. The repository holds only the claim specs; all
  machinery is the pinned research-core library.
